{
  "description": "A regex key that isn't valid is REGEX_ERROR (Format 7.2, 14, 15.3): one that doesn't compile; one with a form outside the shared syntax, such as an inline flag, a lookahead, a backreference, an unescaped bracket, an empty class, a range out of order, a quantifier after a boundary, a zero count or the category Cn; one with a flag other than i, m and s or a repeated flag; one nesting groups more than 100 deep; and one longer than 1000 bytes written out in full. checks/valid-regex-keys.json has the valid keys next to these limits",
  "note": "Written out, (a{10}){n} is (aaaaaaaaaa) n times, 12n bytes: 1008 for n = 84 and 2400 for 200. a{999,} is 999 copies of a then a*, 1001 bytes. The slashes around a key aren't part of its pattern.",
  "bundle": {
